    <statement><p>What is the correct form of the partial fraction decomposition for the following integral? <me>\int \frac{x - 7}{x^3 + 7 x^2 - 8 x} \, dx</me></p>
<p><ol form="buttons" marker="A" name="AnSwEr0001">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int \left( \frac{A}{x - 7} + \frac{B}{x - 8} + \frac{C}{x + 1}  \right)\, dx </m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int \left( \frac{A}{x} + \frac{B}{x - 7} + \frac{C}{x + 1} \right)\, dx </m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>There is no partial fraction decomposition because the denominator does not factor.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int \left( \frac{A x + B}{x} + \frac{C x + D}{x - 1} + \frac{E x + F}{x + 8} \right)\, dx </m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>There is no partial fraction decomposition yet because long division must be done first.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int \left( \frac{A}{x} + \frac{B}{x - 1} + \frac{C}{x + 8} \right)\, dx </m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int \left( \frac{A}{x} + \frac{B x + C}{x - 7} + \frac{D x + E}{x + 1} \right)\, dx </m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>There is no partial fraction decomposition yet because there is cancellation.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{F}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
